  "decision": "An optional global-scope qualifier, then zero or more qualifying segments, then the name itself. The final NAME is not optional, so `A::` is not a qualified name and neither is `$::`.",
  "notes": "The clause's note 3 is explicit that a qualified name does not appear in the abstract syntax at all: what appears is a reference to the element it resolves to. That is why other productions write it in brackets as [QualifiedName]. This production is the text; resolution is a later layer's problem, and ADR-0002 puts an unresolved reference in the IR with its diagnostic rather than rejecting it.",
